hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"166","Al-Haytham bin Ayyub told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, he said: Anba Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing ablution and wiping his head and ears once. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"167","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, who was shown The call, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He performed ablution, washed his face three times, his hands twice, washed his feet twice, and wiped with his head twice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"168","Qutaibah bin Sa`id told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “No prayer will be accepted without purification, nor will charity be accepted without deception.”"
"169","Mahmoud bin Ghailan told us, Ali told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about ablution? So he showed it to him three times, then he said: “This is the ablution. Whoever does more than this has done wrong, transgression and injustice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"170","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hamran, that Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “There is no one who performs ablution and performs his ablution well and then performs the prayer except that his sins between him and the other prayer will be forgiven.” until he prays it\""
171"""
"171","Ishaq ibn Mansur informed us, saying: Ubaydullah informed us, from Shu'bah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, who said: Mu'adh ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, that Humran ibn Aban informed him, saying: I brought water for Uthman to perform wudu; he performed wudu excellently, then said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wudu excellently, then he said: 'Whoever performs wudu like this wudu of mine, then goes to the mosque and prays two rak'ahs therein, his past sins will be forgiven.'"""
"172","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Ibn Amr Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya told me, he said: he told me Muhammad bin Ibrahim, that Shaqiq bin Salamah narrated to him, that Humran said: I saw Uthman perform ablution, then he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He performed an ablution like this one of mine, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs an ablution like this one of mine, then Then he prayed two rak’ahs, and his previous sins were forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"173","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Adam told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, he said: He told me Abu Yahya Salim bin Amer, Damra bin Habib, and Abu Talha Nu`aym bin Ziyad said: We heard Abu Umamah Al-Bahili say: I heard Amr bin Absa, saying: I said: O Messenger of God: How is ablution? He said: “As for ablution, if you perform ablution and wash your palms and purify them, your sins will come out from between your nails and your fingertips. You rinsed your mouth, he said: And you sniffed your nostrils, and you washed your face and your hands up to the elbows, and you wiped your head, and you washed your feet up to the elbows. ankles, you have been washed from all your sins, so if you set your face to God, you will be cleansed of your sins as on the day your mother gave birth to you.”"
"174","Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, he said: Rabi’ah bin Yazid Al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then prays two rak’ahs, reciting them with his heart and face, Paradise is certain for him.”"
"175","Hisham bin Abdul-Malik Abu Taqi al-Homsi told us, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning Ibn Harb, he said: Al-Zubaidi told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. That Omar bin Abdul Aziz told him, that Abdullah bin Qarith told him, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Perform ablution from anything that has touched fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"176","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ismail told us, and Abd al-Razzaq told us, they said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Omar bin Abd. Al-Aziz, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Qarith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “ “Perform ablution from whatever fire has touched.”"
"177","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id told us, he said: Harami, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ja`dah, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Talha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Perform ablution from what fire has changed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"178","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’dah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perform ablution from what fire has dispelled.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"179","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’dah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abd, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perform ablution from what fire has changed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"180","Hisham bin Abdul-Malik told us, he said: Muhammad told us, Al-Zubaidi said, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, that Abdul-Malik bin Abi Bakr He told him that Kharijah bin Zayd bin Thabit told him that Zaid said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Perform ablution \from what the fire touched\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"181","Hisham bin Abdul Malik told us, he said: Ibn Harb told us, he said: Al-Zubaidi told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman He told him, on the authority of Abu Sufyan bin Saeed bin Al-Akhnas bin Shariq, that he informed him, that he had visited the mother of Habiba, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted her, and she was his maternal aunt, so she gave him a drink, then she said to him: “Perform ablution, my sister’s son, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Perform ablution from whatever fire has touched.” Copy that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"182","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja`far, who is the son of Muhammad bin Ali bin Hussein, told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate a shoulder and it came back to him. Bilal went out to pray and did not touch water.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"183","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Left, he said: I went to see Umm Salamah and she told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, and then fast.” And she narrated to us this hadith that she narrated to him: “She brought a roasted lamb to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ate from it. Then he stood up to pray and did not perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"184","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ate bread and meat, then he got up to pray and did not perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"185","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The last of the two commands from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “to abandon ablution from anything that has touched fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"186","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, on the authority of Suwayd bin Al-Nu’man, he said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought a stalk and he ate and we ate with him. Then he rinsed his mouth and stood up and prayed the Maghrib prayer, but he did not perform ablution.”"
"187","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, drank milk, then called for water, rinsed his mouth, and then said: “It has fat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"188","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Aghar, who is Ibn Al-Sabbah, on the authority of Khalifa bin Husayn, On the authority of Qais bin Asim, he converted to Islam and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to “bath himself with water and lotus leaves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"189","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: Thumama bin Examples: Al-Hanafi went to a palm tree near the mosque and took a bath, then he entered the mosque and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness Indeed, Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. O Muhammad, by God, there was no face on earth more hateful to me than your face. Your face has become more beloved to me. All faces are towards me. By God, no religion was more hateful to me than your religion. Your religion has become the religion I love most, by God. A country that is more hateful to me than your country, so your country has become the most beloved to me of all the countries, and your horses took me while I wanted to perform Umrah, so what do you see? “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him the good news and ordered him to perform Umrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"190","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad, who is Ibn Bashar, told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: he told me Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Najia bin Ka’b, on the authority of Ali, who said: When Abu Talib died, I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said to him: Your uncle The lost sheikh had died. He said: “Go and bury him. He died as a polytheist. Go and bury him and do not do anything until you come to me.” So I bury him. Then I came to him and said, ‘I have seen him,’ so he ordered me to wash.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"191","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, he said: I heard Al-Awza’i, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim told me, He says: Al-Qasim bin Muhammad told me, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If circumcision exceeds circumcision, it is obligatory Washing. I and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did it and we washed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"192","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning bin Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, and he said: I heard Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When he sits among its four people, then He worked hard, for it is obligatory to wash.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"193","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told me, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, he said: Ash’ath bin Abdul told us. Al-Malik, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When he sits among its four people, then He worked hard, so it is obligatory to wash.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is wrong, and we do not know of anyone who followed Isa bin Yunus in this, and what is correct is Ash’ath. On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Al-Hasan did not hear from Abu Hurairah, Abu Abdul Rahman said: I doubt"
"194","Qutayba bin Saeed and Ali bin Hajar told us, and the word is for Qutayba. He said: Ubaidah bin Humayd told us, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’, On the authority of Husayn ibn Qabisah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, he said: I was a man who was in trouble, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “If I saw If you have ejaculate, wash your penis and perform your ablution for prayer, and if you spit out water, perform ablution.”"
"195","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Abdul Rahman informed us, on the authority of Zaida, and Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, and the pronunciation for it Abu Al-Walid informed us, Zaida told us, on the authority of Al-Rukin ibn Al-Rabi’ ibn Umaylah Al-Fazari, on the authority of Husayn ibn Qabisah, on the authority of Ali May God be pleased with him. He said: I was a man who was in a state of madhiy, so I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “If you see madhiy, perform ablution and wash your penis. And if you see water gushing out, take a bath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"196","Shuaib bin Yusuf told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, A woman said: O Messenger of God, God is not shy from the truth. Is a woman required to wash herself if she has a wet dream? He said: “Yes, if she sees water.” Umm Salamah laughed and said: Does a woman have a wet dream? Then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “How does the child resemble her?”"
"197","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdah told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that Umm Sulaym asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of a woman who sees in her dreams what a man sees, said: “When water comes out, let her bathe.”"
"198","Kathir bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, that Aisha told him, Umm Sulaym spoke to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while Aisha was sitting, and she said to him: O Messenger of God, God is not ashamed of the truth. Have you ever seen a woman see in a dream what a man sees? Should she take a bath from that? So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Yes.” Aisha said: So I said to her: Is it true for you, or does the woman see that? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to me and said: “Your right hand is crossed, so where does the resemblance come from?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"199","Yusuf bin Sa’id told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Khawla bint Hakim said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a woman having a wet dream, and he said: “If she sees water, let her wash.”"
"200","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Suad, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Water is from water.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"201","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdah told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “A man’s water is thick and white, and a woman’s water is thin and yellow, so whichever of the two comes first is the same.”"
"202","Qutaibah told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Umm Habibah bint asked a fatwa The colt of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, I am undergoing menstruation. He said: “That is only a sweat, so wash and pray.” She used to wash herself for every prayer"
"203","Qutaibah told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of A’rak ibn Malik, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that Umm Habibah asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about blood? She said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, I saw her place filled with blood, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Stay as long as she was.” Your period will stop you, then wash yourself,” Qutaibah told us again, and he did not mention Ja’far."
"204","Imran bin Yazid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abdullah Al-Adawi told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya told us Bin Saeed, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Fatima bint Qais, from the Banu Asad of Quraysh, that she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. She mentioned that she was having menstruation, so she claimed that he had said to her: “That is only a blood clot, so when her period comes, give up prayer.” When you have finished, take a bath and wash off the blood, then pray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"205","Hisham bin Ammar told us, he said: Sahl bin Hashim told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If your menstruation has come, abandon prayer, and if it has come, then take a bath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"206","Imran bin Yazid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abdullah told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Urwah and Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Umm Habibah bint Jahsh had menstruation at the age of seven, so she complained about it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is not menstruation, but this is a sweat, so wash yourself, then pray.”"
"207","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, he said: he told me Al-Numan, Al-Awza’i, and Abu Mu’id, who is Hafs bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr and Amra bint told me Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Umm Habibah bint Jahsh is the wife of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, and she is the sister of Zainab bint Jahsh. So she consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “This is not menstruation, but this A race, so when your period comes, then wash and pray, and when it comes, leave the prayer for it.” Aisha said: She used to wash for every She prayed and prayed, and she would sometimes bathe in a place in her sister Zainab’s room, while she was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until The blood turned red until the water rose, and she came out and prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. What would prevent her from praying?"
"208","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, and Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that Umm Habiba, the circumciser of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the circumciser of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, had her menstruation for seven years. She consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is not menstruation, but This is a sweat, so wash and pray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"209","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that a woman who underwent menstruation at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was told: “It is a stubborn vein,” and she was ordered to delay The noon prayer, and the afternoon prayer hastened, and she should bathe once for them, and the sunset prayer should be delayed, and the evening prayer hastened, and she should bathe once for them. And you bathe once for the morning prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"210","Qutaibah told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Umm Salamah, meaning that a woman used to shed blood on The era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then Umm Salamah consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Let you see the number of nights.” And on the days during the month when she was menstruating before what happened to her afflicted her, she should abandon prayer for an amount of that period of the month. If she missed So let her wash herself, then ask her forgiveness, then pray.”"
"211","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that Umm Habibah bint Jahsh, She had been menstruating for seven years, so she asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “It is not menstruation, rather it is a sweating.” So he ordered her to abandon prayer for the duration of her menstruation and to wash and pray, and she did. “You take a bath at every prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"212","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Mundhir bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Urwa, that Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh narrated that she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and shed blood on him, Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “That is only a vein, so look. If your reading comes to you, do not pray. If your reading has passed, then purify yourself. Then pray, from Qur’an to Qur’an.” This is evidence that Qur’an is menstruation. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He narrated this hadith. Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, and he did not mention about it what Al-Mundhir mentioned."
"213","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdah, Waki’, and Abu Muawiyah told us, they said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, she said. Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I am a woman who is menstruating, but I have not become pure. Should I give up prayer, he said: “No, that is an act of sweating, not menstruation. When your menstruation comes, give up prayer, and when it comes, wash off the blood and pray.”"
"214","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ishaq bin Bakr told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abd. By God, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that Umm Habibah bint Jahsh, who was married to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and that she had had her menstruation had not become pure, so her matter was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “It is not menstruation, but it is A bleeding from the womb, so let her look at the amount of her menstrual cycle, and let her abandon prayer, then she should look for what comes after that and perform ghusl for every prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"215","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Ibn Adiy told us, on the authority of Muhammad, who is the son of Amr bin Alqamah bin Waqqas, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh, said that she used to undergo menstruation, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “If Menstrual blood is black blood and is known to be black, so abstain from praying, and if it is the other blood, then perform ablution, for it is only a vein.” He said: Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us this from his book. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"216","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us from his memorization, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa On the authority of Aisha, that Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh was undergoing menstruation, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “The menstrual blood is black blood.” It is known, so if that is the case, refrain from praying, and if it is the other, then perform ablution and pray.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This was narrated by more than one person. One, none of them mentioned what Ibn Abi Adi mentioned, and God Almighty knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"217","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, saying: Hammad, who is Ibn Zaid, told us on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh had her menstruation, so she asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God. I have menstruation but I am not clean, should I stop praying? The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “That is only an intercourse and is not the menstruation, so when the menstruation approaches, give up prayer, and when it ends, So wash off any traces of blood and perform ablution, for that is a blood clot, and it is not menstruation.” He was told: “Then washing.” He said: “No one doubts that.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know of anyone who mentioned in this hadith “and perform ablution” other than Hammad ibn Zayd, and more than one person narrated it, on the authority of Hisham And it did not mention “performing ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"218","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh said: O Messenger of God, I have not purified myself, should I give up prayer? Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “That is only a period of sweating and is not the menstruation, so when the menstruation comes, give up prayer, and when it goes its value, so wash off the blood and pray.”"
"219","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: I heard Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the daughter of Abi Hubaysh, she said: O Messenger of God, I have not purified myself, should I leave prayer? He said: “No, it is a vein.” He said: Khaled, according to what I read to him, “It is not the menstruation, so if the menstruation comes, give up prayer, and then... “You have turned around, so wash off the blood and pray.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Malik, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, is the most authentic of what comes in The woman suffering from menstruation, and the hadith of Suleiman, on the authority of Umm Salamah, he did not hear it on the authority of Umm Salamah. Among them was a man."
"220","Muhammad ibn Qudamah informed us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, in the hadith of Asma’ bint Umays, when she died in Dhul-Hulayfah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Bakr: “Give her To wash and perform ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"221","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade a man to urinate in stagnant water, then wash himself with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"222","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, on the authority of Ghudayf bin Al-Harith, he said: I went to Aisha and asked her, and I said: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wash himself at the beginning of the night, or at the end of it? She said: “All of that. Perhaps he did ablution at the beginning, and perhaps he did a ritual ablution at the end.” I said: Praise be to God who made the matter sufficient."
"223","Amr bin Hisham told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Nasi, on the authority of Ghudayf ibn Al-Harith He asked Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on what night the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to take a bath. She said: “Maybe he took a bath on the first night, and perhaps he took a bath at the end of it.” I said: Praise be to God, who has made the matter expansive."
"224","Mujahid bin Musa told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Yahya bin al-Walid told me, he said: Mahal bin Khalifa told me, he said: Abu Al-Samh told me, he said: I was serving the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he wanted to wash himself, he would say: “I have your back, so give it to me.” My back, so I cover him with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"225","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Abu Murrah, the servant of Aqeel bin Abi Talib. On the authority of Umm Hani, that she went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the conquest, and found him bathing and Fatima covering him with a garment. So I greeted him, and he said: “Who is this?” I said: Umm Hani, so when he finished washing him, he got up and prayed eight rak’ahs in a garment, wrapped in it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"226","Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Yahya bin Zakaria told us, on the authority of Musa Al-Juhani, he said: A Mujahid came with a cup of which I guessed eight Pounds, and he said: Aisha told me: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bathe like this.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"227","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. “He bathes in a cup, and that is the difference.”"
"228","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, I heard Abu Salamah, He says: I went to see Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and her breastfeeding brother, and he asked her about the bathing of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? “So she called for a vessel containing water equal to a saa’ of water, and she covered herself with a veil, then she bathed and poured water on her head three times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"229","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said: We practiced washing at Jabir bin Abdullah. Jabir said: “A saa’ of water is sufficient for ablution from ritual impurity.” We said: Neither a saa’ nor two saa’s is sufficient. Jabir said: “It is sufficient for whoever is better than you and has more poetry.”"
"230","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “I and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wash from one vessel.”"
"231","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: Muammar and Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “I and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wash from one vessel, which is the size of the difference.”"
"232","Qutaibah informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He and I wash from one vessel from which we all take a drink.”"
"233","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Qasim told me, he said: I heard Al-Qasim, narrating, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wash from one vessel for ritual impurity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"234","Yahya bin Musa told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: My aunt Maimunah told me That she and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bathe from one vessel."
"235","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yazid, he said: I heard Abdul Rahman bin Hurmuz Al-Araj, saying: Na’im, the servant of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, narrated to me that Umm Salamah was asked: Should a woman bathe with a man? She said: Yes, if it is dirty, you will see me and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taking a bath from one place, pouring water on our hands until We will purify them, then pour water over them.” Al-Araj said: “Do not mention private parts, and do not care about them.”"
"236","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Dawud Al-Awdi, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I met a man He accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, just as Abu Hurairah accompanied him for four years. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade combing One of us every day, or he urinates in his bath, or the man bathes with the grace of the woman, or the woman with the grace of the man, and let them all wash.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"237","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Mu’adh, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I was taking a bath. And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from one vessel, and he hastened with me and I hastened with him, until he said: Leave for me, and I said: Leave for me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"238","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Umm Hani, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “he and Maimunah took a bath from a single vessel in a bowl that had traces of dough in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"239","Suleiman bin Mansour informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rafi’, on the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I said: O Messenger of God, I am a woman who has a tight braid on my head. Shall I undo it when To wash him from impurity? He said: “It is enough for you to pour three handfuls of water over your head, then pour it over your body.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"240","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Al-Nadr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib told us, he said: I heard Abu Salamah He entered upon Aisha and asked her about washing the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from ritual impurity? She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would bring a vessel and pour it on his hands three times, then pour it with his right hand on his left and wash off what was on it.” His thighs, then he washes his hands, rinses his mouth, sniffs, and pours water over his head three times, then pours water over his entire body.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"241","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Omar bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ata bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, he said: She described Aisha reported that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, washed during ritual impurity. She narrated, “He would wash his hands three times, then spread his right hand over the left.” Then he should wash his private parts and whatever touched it.” Omar said: I do not know him except that he said: Then he should wash his right hand over his left three times, then rinse his mouth three times. He inhales three times, washes his face and hand three times, then pours water over his head three times, then pours water over him."
"242","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, When he performed ritual ablution due to ritual impurity, he would begin by washing his hands, then perform ablution as he performs ablution for prayer, then he would insert his fingers into the water and mix them with them. the roots of his hair, and pour three scoops of water over his head, then pour the water over all of his skin,” on the authority of Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Sadaqa bin Saeed al-Hanafi, on the authority of Juma bin Umair, who said: My mother and aunt entered the Aisha, and one of them asked her: How did you do your washing? Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform his ablution for prayer, then pour over his head three times, and we used to pour over his head three times. on our heads five for the sake of plaiting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"243","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sulayman bin Surad, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mut’im, he said: They discussed washing with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and some of the people said: I will wash such-and-such, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “As for me, I spread three palms over my head.”"
"244","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Miswar Al-Zuhri informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, that a woman asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about her ritual ablution after menstruation? So he told her how to wash herself. He said: “Take some musk and purify yourself with it.” She said: How do I purify yourself with it? So he covered such-and-such, then he said: “Glory be to God, purify yourself with it.” Aisha said: So I pulled the woman, and Aisha said: You should follow with it. trace of blood (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"245","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim informed us, he said: My father informed us, he said: Hasan informed us, and he is Ibn Salih bin Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “does not perform ablution after washing.”"
"246","Ali bin Hajar bin Iyas told us, he said: Abba Issa, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: My aunt told me Maimuna, she said: “I approached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to wash him from impurity.” So he washed his hands two or three times, then entered his right hand. In the vessel, he poured it onto his private parts, then he washed it with his left hand, then he struck the ground with his left hand and rubbed it vigorously, then he performed ablution. He performed his ablution for prayer, then he poured three handfuls of water over his head, filling his palms, then he washed the rest of his body, then he moved away from his place and washed His feet, she said: “Then I brought him the handkerchief and he spread it,” and on the authority of Yusuf ibn Isa, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Musa, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and something similar to it."
"247","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Kurayb, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “took a bath, and a handkerchief was brought, but he did not touch it and left, saying: With water like this.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"248","Humayd bin Masada informed us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Habib, on the authority of Shu’bah, and Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: Yahya told us, And Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He said, “If he wants to eat or sleep while he is in a state of state, he should perform his ablution for prayer.” Amr added in his hadith: His ablution is for prayer."
"249","Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “if he wanted to sleep while he was in his state, he would perform ablution, and if he wanted If he eats, he washes his hands.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"250","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution if he wanted to sleep while he was in a state of ritual ablution, and if he wanted to eat or drink She said: He washed his hands, then he ate and drank."
"251","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said that he was in a state of ritual impurity during the night, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perform ablution and wash your private parts, then sleep.”"
"252","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hisham bin Abdul-Malik told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, and Ubaid Allah bin told us Saeed, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Ibn Naji, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Angels do not enter a house in which there is an image, nor a dog, nor a junub.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"253","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “If one of you wants to return, he should perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"254","Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, and the wording is for Ishaq. He said: Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Humaid, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “went around his wives one night with one ritual bath.”"
"255","Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Muammar informed us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “circulate around his wives in one bath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"256","Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: Abba Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, He said: Two men and I came to Ali, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come out of the toilet and recite the Qur’an and eat with us. Meat, and nothing blocked it from the Qur’an. It is not impurity.”"
"257","Muhammad ibn Ahmad Abu Yusuf al-Saydali al-Raqqi informed us, saying: Issa ibn Yunus narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, On the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to recite the Qur’an in every state except during ritual impurity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"258","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, told us, he said: Humayd told us, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, met him on one of the roads of Medina, while he was in a state of impurity, so he slipped out and went and took a bath, so the Prophet lost him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When he came to him, he said: “Where have you been, Abu Hurairah?” He said: “O Messenger of God, you met me while I was standing beside you, so I hated to meet you.” He sat with you until he washed, and he said: “Glory be to God, the believer does not become impure.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"259","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abba Yahya, he said: Mas’ar told us, he said: Wasil told me, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, met him while he was junub, and he fell in love with me. I said: I am junub. He said: “The believer is not impure.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"260","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when a man met one of his companions, he wiped him and prayed for him, saying: I saw him one day early and turned away from him, then I came to him when he rose. During the day, he said: “I saw you and you turned away from me.” He said: “I was in a state of ritual impurity, so I was afraid that you would touch me.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A Muslim is not impure.”"
"261","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah informed us, and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Give me the wine from the mosque.” So I said: I am menstruating, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your menstruation is not in your control.” This is the hadith of Jarir, and Abu Muawiyah is like him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"262","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Manbouth, on the authority of his mother, that Maimuna said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He places his head on one of us’s lap and recites the Qur’an while she is menstruating, and one of us carries her veil to the mosque, and she spreads it while she is \menstruating\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"263","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Mukhlid bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh and Ali bin Hajar bin Iyas informed us, and the pronunciation is for him. He said: I am Sufyan. On the authority of Mansour, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on the lap of one of us while she was menstruating. And he was reciting the Qur’an.”"
"264","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, Sufyan told us, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to nod to me with his head while he was in Itikaf, so I would wash him while I was menstruating.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"265","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I was moving the head of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I am menstruating.” I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, and Ali bin Shuaib told us, he said: Ma’an told us, He said: Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, similar to that."
"266","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh bin Hani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Shurayh, that He asked Aisha: Should a woman eat with her husband while she is menstruating? She said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to invite me to eat with him while I was naked, and he used to take the arak and divide some of it among me. So I sweat some of it, then put it on, and he takes some of it and puts some of the sweat in his mouth where I put my mouth, and he calls for a drink and swears by me. in it before he drank from it, so I took it and drank from it, then I put it down and he took it and drank from it and put his mouth where I put mine. \the mug\"""""
"267","Ayoub bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abdullah bin Jafar told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Miqdam Ibn Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to put his mouth on the place from which I would drink.” And he drank from the leftovers of my drink while I was menstruating.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"268","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Aisha, may God be pleased with her, says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to hand me a vessel and I would drink from it while I was menstruating, then I would give it to him.” Then he will find out where my mouth is and put it on his mouth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"269","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: He told us Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, that Zainab, the daughter of Umm Salamah, narrated, that Umm Salama narrated to her, she said: While I was lying with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the tent, so I slipped out of the quilt, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Have you had a breath?” So I said: Yes. So he called me, and I lay with him in the tent.”"
"270","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Hisham told us, and Ubayd Allah bin Saeed and Ishaq bin Ibrahim, they said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, and the pronunciation is his. He said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah told us, that Zainab was the daughter of Umm Salamah told him that Umm Salamah told her, she said: While I was lying with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the tent, When I menstruated, I slipped out and took my menstrual clothes, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Have you had a breath?” I said: Yes, so he called me and I lay with him. \in the hamlet\"""""
"271","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Subh, he said: I heard Khalas, speaking, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I spent the night in the same place while I was menstruating. If any of my semen got on it, he washed its place without He would return it and pray in it, then come back and if something befalls him, he would do the same and wash its place. He would not return it and pray in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"272","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “It was “When one of us menstruates, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commands her to cover herself, then he will have intercourse with her.”"
"273","Qutaibah told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “commands one of us, if she is menstruating, to tighten her lower garment, then he will have intercourse with her.”"
"274","Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, he read it to him, and I heard, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, and Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Habib was the servant of Urwa, on the authority of Badiyya, and Al-Layth said: Nadba was the servant of Maimunah, she said: On the authority of Maimunah, she said: He was the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “may have intercourse with one of his wives while she is menstruating if she is wearing a garment that reaches halfway up the thighs and the knees.” “In the hadith of Al-Layth: she detained him"
"275","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sulayman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: When a woman was menstruating, the Jews did not eat with them, did not drink with them, and did not have intercourse with them in their homes. So they asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: And they ask you about menstruation. Say, “It is a harm.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded them. He granted “that they may eat with them, drink with them, and have intercourse with them in the houses, and that they may do everything to them except sexual intercourse.” So the Jews said: What? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would abandon any of our affairs unless he disagreed with us, so Usayd ibn al-Hudair and Abbad ibn Bishr stood up and informed the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and they said: Let us have intercourse with them during menstruation. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, began to sweat so intensely that we thought that he had He became angry with them, so they got up, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, received a gift of milk, so he sent after them, brought them back, and gave them to drink. So they knew that he was not angry with them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"276","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Al-Hakam Ibn Utaiba told me, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid, on the authority of Divided, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding a man having intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: “He gives in charity a dinar, or \For half a dinar\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"277","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: We went out With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we only do Hajj. When it was at Saraf, I menstruated and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me and I was crying. He said: “What is the matter with you? Have you had enough?” I said: Yes, and he said: “This is a command that God has decreed for the daughters of Adam, so perform what the Hajj performs, unless you do not perform tawaf.” At home.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed cows on behalf of his wives."
"278","Amr bin Ali, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, and the word is Ya’qub, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said Ja`far bin Muhammad told us, he said: My father told me, he said: We came to Jabir bin Abdullah and asked him about the proof of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he told us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out for the remaining five days of Dhu al-Qa`dah, and we went out with him until Dhu al-Hulayfah gave birth. Asma bint Umays, known as Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, sent a message to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: What should I do? He said: “Wash and ask yourself, then go to my family.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"279","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima bint Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a fatwa about menstrual blood getting on the clothes? He said: “Groom it and pinch it, then offer it a sacrifice and pray in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"280","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Al-Miqdam Thabit Al-Haddad told me, on the authority of Adi bin A dinar. He said: I heard Umm Qays bint Muhsin that she asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about menstrual blood getting on the clothes? He said: “Rub it on the rib and wash it with water and lotus leaves.”"
"281","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Anba Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qais, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Hudayj, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Abi Sufyan, that he asked Umm Habiba, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray in a garment? The one who has intercourse with him? She said: “Yes, as long as he does not see any harm in him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"282","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I was “I wash off the garment of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the garment of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he goes out to pray, and there are spots of water on his garment.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"283","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majlaz, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Nawfal, on the authority of Aisha She said: “I was rubbing semen from the garment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"284","Shuaib bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I used to see him in a garment. Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I scratched it, semen.”"
"285","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Umm Qais bint Muhsin, she brought a young son of hers who did not eat food to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made him sit. And he said hello in his lap, but he urinated on his garment, so he called for water and sprinkled it on it, but he did not wash it.”"
"286","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought “Then he urinated on his garment, so he called for water and he followed it.”"
"287","Mujahid bin Musa told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Yahya bin al-Walid told me, he said: Mahal bin Mahdi told me, Caliph, he said: Abu Al-Samh told me, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He washes with the urine of a female slave, and sprinkles with the urine of a boy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"288","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, he said: Qatada told us, that Anas bin Malik He told them that people or men from Ukal came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and spoke Islam. They said: O Messenger of God, we They were the people of Dara’, and we were not the people of the countryside, and they settled in the city.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to bring animals and a shepherd. He ordered them to go out into it and drink its milk and urine. When they woke up and were near Al-Harra, they disbelieved after their conversion to Islam. They killed the shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and led the sheep. Then the news reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he sent the request among their followers, so he came. They gouged out their eyes and cut off their hands and feet, then left them in the free country as they were until they died.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"289","Muhammad bin Wahb bin Abi Karimah al-Harrani told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahim told me, he said: he told me Zayd bin Abi Unaisah, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: Bedouins from ‘Urinah came to the Prophet God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So they converted to Islam and invaded Medina until their colors turned yellow and their stomachs became heavy, so the Prophet of God sent them May God bless him and grant him peace, to a vaccine for him, “So he commanded them to drink from its milk and its urine, until they recovered and killed its herdsmen and drank from it.” Camels, so the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent for them, and he brought them, cut off their hands and feet, and gouged out their eyes,” he said. Abdul-Malik, to Anas, while he was telling him this hadith, was it disbelief or sin? He said: With disbelief. Abu Abdul Rahman said: We do not know of anyone. He said: On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, in this hadith. Other than Talha bin Musrif, and what is correct with us, and God knows best, is Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, mursal (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"290","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Ali, who is Ibn Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun said: Abdullah told us, in the treasury, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying at the house, and a crowd of The Quraysh were sitting and had slaughtered a camel, and some of them said: Which of you takes this dung with his blood, then gives it time until he lays his face prostrating? Then he placed it on his back. Abdullah said: Then the most miserable of hers ran up and took the dung and carried it away. Then he gave him some time until he fell down prostrating and placed it on his back. His back, so I informed Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was a slave girl, and she came running and took him from his back, so when He finished his prayer and said: “O God, bless the Quraysh three times, O God, bless Abu Jahl bin Hisham and Shaybah bin Rabi’ah.” And Utba bin Rabi’ah, and Uqba bin Abi Mu’ait, until he counted seven of the Quraysh. Abdullah said: By the one to whom the Book was revealed, I saw them killed on the day of Badr in one heart."
"291","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Anba Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “took the limb of His cloak and he spat on it and some of it spread over another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"292","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Al-Qasim bin Mihran, narrating on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you prays, he should not spit in front of his hands, nor on his right, but on his left or Under his feet.” Otherwise, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would have spit on his garment like this and rubbed it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"293","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “We went out with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during some of his travels, until we were in Al-Bayda, or in the same army, a contract with me was broken, so the Messenger of May God bless him and grant him peace upon his petition, and the people stayed with him and they were not on water and they had no water with them, so the people came to Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, they said: Do you not see what Aisha did? She stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with the people, and they were not on water, and they had no water. Then Abu Bakr came and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was laying his head on my thigh while he had fallen asleep. He said: I imprisoned the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted the people, and they were not on water and they had no water with them. She said: Aisha. Then Abu Bakr blamed me and said: What God willed him to say, and made He stabbed my waist with his hand, and nothing prevented me from moving except where the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on my thigh. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell asleep. May God bless him and grant him peace, until the morning became without water. Then God revealed the verse about tayammum, and they performed tayammum. Usayd ibn al-Hudayr said: What is the first of your blessings? O family of Abu Bakr, we sent away the camel that I was riding and found the knot beneath it.”"
"294","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: “The Messenger of God married May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, at the beginning of the army, and with him was Aisha, and her necklace was cut off due to the fear of Dhufar, so people kept trying to necklace her, until The dawn had come, and the people had no water, so Abu Bakr became angry with her and said: You imprisoned the people and they had no water, so God sent down a concession. Purification in the good plain, so the Muslims stood up with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and struck the ground with their hands, then they raised their hands and did not They grabbed some dirt, so they wiped their faces and their hands to the palms, and from the palms of their hands to the armpits.” Malik bin Anas disagreed with him: he narrated it on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ammar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"295","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Asma’ told us, on the authority of Juwayriyah, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, that he informed him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: “We performed tayammum with the Messenger of God May God bless him and grant him peace, with dust, so we wiped our faces and our hands to the shoulders.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Both of them are preserved, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"296","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Abu Malik, and on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abza, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abza, he said: We were with Omar and a man came to him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, We only stayed for a month or two months and did not find water. Omar said: As for me, if I did not find water, I would not pray until I found water. He said Ammar bin Yasser: Do you remember, O Commander of the Faithful, when you were in such-and-such a place, and we were herding camels, so you would know that we were in a state of ritual impurity? He said: Yes. As for me, I rolled in the dirt, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he laughed and said: “If the desert were sufficient for you, and he struck with his palms until the ground, then he blew on them, then wiped his face and some of his arms. He said: Fear God, O Ammar. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, if you wish, you may not I remember him. He said: No, but we will give you of that what you have assumed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"297","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, that a man came to Omar and said: I have entered the state of ritual impurity, but I could not find water. He said: Do not pray, so Ammar bin Yasser said: O Amir. Believers, remember when you and I were in a troop, and we set out and did not find water. As for you, you did not pray, and as for me, I was covered in dirt. So I prayed, so we came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we mentioned that to him, and he said: “It was enough for you.” He placed his hands on the ground and then blew. So he wiped his face and hands with them. Salama doubted: I don’t know whether it was up to the elbows or up to the palms, so Omar said: We will give you of that what you have undertaken. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"298","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abd Al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, that a man asked Omar bin Al-Khattab about tayammum, but he did not know what to say, so Ammar said: Do you not remember where We were on a expedition, and I became junub and buried myself in the dirt, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “This is enough for you,” and he struck. Shu`bah placed his hands on his knees, blew on his hands, and wiped his face and palms with them once.”"
"299","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim Al-Massi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Salamah, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Ibn Abd Al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, that a man came to Omar, may God be pleased with him, and said: I entered the state of ritual impurity and did not find water, so Omar said: Do not pray. Ammar said: O Commander of the Faithful, do you not remember that you and I were in a expedition, and we went out into a state of ritual impurity, but we did not find water, and as for you, you did not pray. So I immersed myself in the dirt, then prayed. When we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I mentioned that to him, and he said: “It is enough for you.” And he struck The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his hands on the ground, then he blew on them and wiped his face and palms with them. Salama doubted and said: I do not know about him until The elbows, or up to the palms. Omar said: We will give you of that what you have been given. Shu’bah said: He used to say: the palms, the face, and the arms. Mansour said to him: What you say, because no one mentions the arms except you. Salama became doubtful, so he said: I do not know whether he mentioned the arms or not. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"300","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning bin Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ammar bin Yasser, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He commanded him to perform tayammum for the face.” And the two palms”"
"301","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hormuz, on the authority of Umayr, the client of Ibn Abbas, that he heard him say: I and Abdullah bin Yasar, the client of Maimuna, approached until we entered to Abu Jahm ibn al-Harith ibn al-Sammah. Abu al-Jahm said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from the direction of the Camel Well and met him. A man greeted him, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not respond until he approached the wall. “So he wiped his face and hands, then returned his greetings to him.”"
"302","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah, and my father Musa, then Abu Musa said: Did you not hear Ammar say to Omar: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me for a need, but I ran away but could not find anything. water, so I wallowed in the plains, then I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned that to him, and he said: “It was enough for you to say Thus, then he struck his hand on the ground once, then wiped his palm and shook it off. Then he struck his left hand on his right, and his right on his right. His left hand is on his palms and his face.” Abdullah said: Have you not seen that Omar was not satisfied with Ammar’s statement? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"303","Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Najia bin Khafaf, on the authority of Ammar bin Yasser, he said: I was in a state of impurity while I was with the camels, but I did not find water, so I wandered in the dirt like an animal does, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I told him about that, and he said: “It was only to reward you for that tayammum.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"304","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Raja, he said: I heard Imran bin Husayn that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a secluded man who did not pray with the people, so he said: “O so-and-so, what prevented you from praying with the people?” So he said: “O.” The Messenger of God was afflicted with impurity and there was no water, so he said: “You should go to the desert land, for it is sufficient for you.”"
"305","Amr bin Hisham told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Amr bin Bojdan, on the authority of Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pure earth is the ablution of a Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years.”"
"306","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Abu Muawiyah, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Usayd ibn Hudair and some people to ask for a necklace that Aisha had forgotten in a guest house where she stayed, so she came. Prayer without performing ablution, and they did not find water, so they prayed without ablution. They mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God revealed The verse of tayammum. Usayd ibn Hudair said: May God reward you with good. By God, no matter has happened to you that you dislike except that God will make it good for you and for the Muslims. \""
307"""
"307","Isma'il ibn Mas'ud informed us, saying: Yazid ibn Zura'i narrated to us, saying: Hisham — meaning ibn Abi 'Abdullah — and Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Qatadah narrated to us, saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, from Malik ibn Sa'sa'ah, that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: ""While I was at the House (Ka'bah), in a state between sleep and wakefulness, one of the three (angels) came to me between the two men. I was brought a golden basin filled with wisdom and faith. He split (my chest) from the throat to the upper part of the abdomen, then washed the heart with Zamzam water. Then it was filled with wisdom and faith. I was brought a white beast, smaller than a mule and larger than a donkey, called al-Buraq. I set out with Jibril until we reached the lowest heaven. It was asked: 'Who is this?' It was said: 'Jibril.' It was asked: 'And who is with you?' It was said: 'Muhammad.' It was asked: 'Has he been sent for?' It was said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Welcome to him; excellent is his coming.' So I came upon Adam and greeted him. He said: 'Welcome, O righteous son and Prophet.' Then we ascended to the second heaven... [the narration continues through the seven heavens, meeting prophets, until the Sidrat al-Muntaha, the obligation of fifty prayers, reduction to five after consultation with Musa, and the promise of tenfold reward for each good deed]."" Abu 'Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Zuhri narrated this hadith, and al-Zuhri differed from Qatadah in its chain and text. Ibn Wahb narrated it from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from Abu Dharr. Some companions of Yunus narrated it from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from Ubayy — and this is an error; it resembles that ""Dharr"" dropped from the book, becoming ""from Abi,"" so it was thought to be Ubayy. This hadith was also narrated from al-Zuhri, from Anas (without mention of Malik ibn Sa'sa'ah or Abu Dharr), and Thabit narrated it from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, without mentioning Malik ibn Sa'sa'ah or Abu Dharr."
"308","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Abba Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: Abu Dharr used to narrate that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The roof of my house was parted while I was in Mecca, and Gabriel came down and parted my chest, then He washed it with Zamzam water, then brought it a golden basin full of wisdom and faith, and placed it on my chest, then closed it, then took my hand. Then he took me up to heaven.” He narrated the hadith, and said: Ibn Hazm and Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has enjoined upon my nation fifty prayers, so I returned That is until he ordered Moses, and Moses said: What has your Lord enjoined upon your nation? I said: He has enjoined upon them fifty prayers. Moses said to me: So return to your Lord. Your nation cannot tolerate that, so I went back to my Lord, and He placed half of it. So I returned to Moses and told him, and he said: Return to your Lord, for your nation cannot tolerate that. So I went back to my Lord, and he said: It is five, and it is fifty. The word I have cannot be changed. So I returned to Moses, and he said: Go back to your Lord, and I said: I have become ashamed. From my Lord"
"309","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told me, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Malik bin Mughul told us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Talha Ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was taken on the journey, he ended up at Sidra al-Muntaha. And it is in the sixth heaven. To it ends what comes out from below it and to it ends what descends from it from above it until it is caught from it. He said: When the sidra was covered with something that covered it, he said: A bed of gold, and three things were given to him: the five daily prayers, and the endings of Surat Al-Baqarah. And He will be forgiven whomever of his nation who dies not associating anything with God.”"
"310","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id told him while he was Thabit bin Aslam, that Al-Bunani told him, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that “Prayer was made obligatory in Mecca, and that two angels came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” May God bless him and grant him peace. So they took him to Zamzam, cut open his stomach, and took out his stuffing in a golden basin. They washed it with Zamzam water, then They stuffed his belly with wisdom and faith.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id, Yahya bin Sa’id, and Sa’d bin Sa’id bin Qays. Ibn Fahd Al-Ansari, who are three brothers, and Yahya Ibn Saeed, the most distinguished and noble of them, and he is one of the imams, and he is not in Medina. Al-Zuhri was more distinguished in his time than him, and the servant of his Lord is trustworthy, and Sa’d is weak."
"311","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “Prayer was made obligatory as two rak’ahs.” Then the travel prayer was established and the urban prayer was added.”"
"312","Amr bin Ali told us, Yahya told us, and Abdul Rahman told us, they said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Prayer was enjoined by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to be four rak’ahs in the city, two rak’ahs when traveling, and one rak’ah in fear.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"313","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Suhail, on the authority of his father, that he heard Talha bin Ubaid Allah say: A man came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was from the people of Najd. He had a broken head, the sound of his voice could be heard, and he did not understand what he was saying. Until he approached, he was He asked about Islam, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Five prayers per day and night.” He said: Do I have to do anything else? He said: “No, unless you do it voluntarily.” He said: “And fasting the month of Ramadan.” He said: Do I have to do anything else? He said: “No, unless you do it voluntarily.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned zakat to him. He said: Do I have to pay anything else? He said: “No, unless you do it voluntarily.” Then the man turned away and said: By God, I will neither add to this nor take away from it. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “He will succeed if he is truthful.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Abu Sa’id is the uncle of Malik ibn Anas, and his name is Nafi’ ibn Malik ibn Abu Aamer Al-Asbahi, who is one of the trustworthy"
"314","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Mushar told us, he said: Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani, said: The beloved and trustworthy Awf bin Malik narrated to me, saying: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said: “Will you not pledge allegiance?” He repeated it three times, so we presented our hands and pledged our allegiance to him, so we said: O Messenger of God, we have pledged our allegiance to you, so we did so. ? He said: “On the condition that you worship God and do not associate anything with Him, and the five daily prayers, and he concealed a hidden word, ‘Do not ask the people anything.’” Abu Abdul Rahman: Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, his name is Aid Allah bin Abdullah, and Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani, his name is: Abdullah bin Thub"
"315","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Qais told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, He said: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to establish prayer, pay zakat, and advise every Muslim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"316","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, and his name is Abdullah, that a man from Banu Kinana called Al-Mukhadji heard a man in the Levant, nicknamed Abu Muhammad, say: The Witr prayer is obligatory. He said Al-Mukhadji: I went to Ubadah ibn al-Samit and stopped by him while he was going to the mosque, so I told him what Abu Muhammad said, and he said Worship: Abu Muhammad lied. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There are five prayers that God has prescribed for His servants, so whoever comes By them, he did not waste any of them, by belittling their rights. He had a covenant with God that He would admit him to Paradise, and whoever did not bring them does not have them. “There is a covenant with God. If He wills, He will admit him to Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"317","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Have you seen that if there was a river at the door of one of you in which he would bathe five times every day, would he “Is there anything left of his dirt?” They said: “There is nothing left of his dirt.” He said: “That is like the five daily prayers. With them, God erases sins.” He said: Abu Abd al-Rahman: Ibn al-Had’s name is Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usama ibn al-Had, and Abu Salamah’s name is Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Awf, and Abu Hurairah, his name is Abd Amr, and it is said that Abd Shams, and it is said that Sakīn, and he said: Sufyan Ibn Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Muharrir bin Abi Hurairah said: Abu’s name is Abd Amr bin Abd Ghanam. We told him Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Bakr bin Bakkar, on the authority of Omar bin Ali bin Muqaddam, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Abu Abdul Rahman said: Bakr bin Bakkar is not strong in hadith. Sufyan bin Hussein is not strong in Al-Zuhri in particular, and in other matters there is nothing wrong with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"318","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The delegation of Abdul Qais came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he commanded them to do four things: “To believe in God alone, to establish prayer, and to perform zakat, fast Ramadan, and be given from the five spoils.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"319","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba al-Nadr ibn Shumail, he said: Anba Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of al-Azraq ibn Qais, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ya`mar. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The first thing a servant will be held accountable for is his prayer. If he completes it, otherwise God said: Look for My servant to do voluntary prayers. If any voluntary prayer is found for him, He will say: Complete the obligatory prayer with him."
"320","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Harun Al-Khazzaz told us, Hammam said: On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Harith bin Qabisah, he said: I came to Medina and said: Oh God, facilitate a good companion for me, so I sat with Abu Hurairah and said: I prayed to God to facilitate a good companion for me. So he told me a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Perhaps God would benefit me with it. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he says: “The first thing a servant will be held accountable for is his prayers. If they are good, he has prospered and succeeded, and if they are bad, then he has been disappointed and lost,” Hammam said. I do not know whether this is from the words of Qatada, or from the narration: And if he detracted from his obligatory prayer in any way, he would say: Look, does My servant do anything voluntary? He completes what is missing from the obligatory prayer, and then the rest of his work is in the same manner."
"321","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Suleiman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, A man received a kiss from a woman, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have not repented, so I came down and performed prayer at two ends of the day. Early in the night, he recited the verse, and the man said: Is it for me? He said: “It is for those of my nation who act upon it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"322","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abba Isa bin Yunus, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, he said: I heard Hudhayfah, saying: We were with Omar, He said: Which of you memorizes the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding temptation? I said: I remember what he said. He said: You are bold against him. So come, and I said: “A man’s temptation against his family, his neighbor, and his wealth is expiated by prayer, charity, and enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong.” He said: I am not asking you about this, but I am asking you about that which waves like the waves of the sea. So I said: Do not be afraid, O Commander of the Faithful, for There is a closed door between you and her"
"323","Muhammad bin Uthman told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Uthman told us, and his father Uthman bin Abdullah, that they heard Musa bin Talha, speaking, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that a man said: O Messenger of God, inform me of a job that will enable me to enter Paradise. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Worship God and do not associate anything with Him, and perform prayer, and maintain the ties of kinship as if it had been \His mount\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"324","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The covenant between us and them is prayer, so whoever abandons it has disbelieved.”"
"325","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Perhaps you will come across people who pray the prayer outside of its time, so if you catch them, they will perform the prayer at its time.” And pray with them and make it a rosary.”"
"326","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rabi’ah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “There is nothing between a servant and disbelief except abandonment of prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"327","Harun bin Abdullah informed us, Abu Dawud said, he said: Muhammad bin Muslim bin Abi Al-Wadah informed us, on the authority of Abdul Karim Al-Jazari, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray before noon after noon. Four rak'ahs, and he says: The gates of heaven are opened, so I like to perform righteous deeds therein. Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Abd Al-Karim Al-Jazari, he is Abd Al-Karim bin Malik, trustworthy, and Abd Al-Karim Al-Basri, he is Abd Al-Karim bin Al-Muharriq, nothing. He is called Abu Umayyah, Mujahid bin Jabr is Abu Al-Hajjaj, and Ibn Ishaq says: Ibn Jubayr, and the correct one is Ibn Jabr. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"328","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, said: When the sun had set, the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would pray four rak’ahs before noon, when it set. \the sun\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"329","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin al-Muntashir told me, on the authority of his father On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would not omit four rak’ahs before noon and two rak’ahs before morning.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"330","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Amr told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “he would pray two rak’ahs before noon, two rak’ahs after noon, two rak’ahs after sunset, and after \Isha' is two rak'ahs\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
